  "cards": [
    {"dot": "cyan", "title": "Shared storage does not imply shared semantics", "items": ["All three mechanisms can produce alert history, but their detector identifiers, evidence and observation times mean different things (docs/network-detections.md:5-13).", "Network-detection alerts are not linked as YAML rule alerts by related-record linking. Inspect the detector-specific evidence rather than assuming every alert names a matched audit record (docs/network-detections.md:50; docs/evidence.md:29-36)."]},
    {"dot": "amber", "title": "No alert is only meaningful within coverage", "items": ["Built-in network detection is on by default; operator-supplied IP/domain indicators need their own source, version and validity interval. No threat-intelligence feed or STIX/TAXII ingestion is bundled (docs/network-detections.md:3,36-40).", "Queue overflow and late application observations qualify network findings. Some application evidence appears only at completion or checkpoints (docs/network-detections.md:23-34).", "Behavior learns candidates before explicit approval; it cannot infer trust from learning. Unknown capture-health counters remain unknown (docs/behavioral-monitoring.md:3,71-80)."]},
